WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.480
There's nothing surprising about most sequels
these days — especially since they seem

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.550
to be a dime a dozen.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:09.710
Thankfully, though, there are at least a handful
of upcoming projects that nobody could have

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:10.870
seen coming.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.120
These are some of the movie sequels you probably
didn't know are happening.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.130
Before Zack Snyder's bloody zombie heist film
Army of the Dead had even premiered on Netflix

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:24.440
in 2021, the movie's producers were already
looking ahead to the future of the franchise.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.180
While the ending of the film didn't seem to
leave a lot of room for sequels, the opening

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:33.700
sequences suggested plenty of potential backstory
to mine — and that's exactly what Netflix

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.700
is planning.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.960
In addition to an anime series tracing the
early days of the zombie outbreak, titled

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.260
Army of the Dead: Lost Vegas, the 2021 film
will also receive a prequel feature centered

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.839
around its expert safe-cracker, Ludwig Dieter.

00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:52.010
Titled Army of Thieves, the prequel will be
directed by Matthias Schweighöfer, who will

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.440
also star as the scene-stealing criminal.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.850
The film will be set just as the zombies are
first spreading across Las Vegas, an event

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:02.999
shown only as a quick, epic montage at the
beginning of Army of the Dead.

00:01:02.999 --> 00:01:07.620
According to Snyder, it will primarily tell
the story of how Dieter's safe-cracking career

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.890
came to be.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:13.869
Like Army of the Dead, Army of Thieves will
also feature an ensemble cast, although Schweighöfer

00:01:13.869 --> 00:01:16.490
will be the only carryover from the first
film.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:21.850
Joining him for the prequel will be Nathalie
Emmanuel, Guz Khan, Ruby O. Fee, and Stuart

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:22.850
Martin.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:26.609
While Netflix hasn't yet given the film a
precise premiere date, it's set to hit the

00:01:26.609 --> 00:01:28.280
streamer sometime in 2021.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:34.340
Long before John Boyega was fighting the First
Order in Star Wars, he was fighting far more

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:38.439
monstrous aliens in the urban sci-fi adventure
Attack the Block.

00:01:38.439 --> 00:01:43.430
Written and directed by Joe Cornish, the 2011
film starred Boyega as Moses, the leader of

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:48.329
a South London street gang that decides to
rid their neighborhood of vicious extraterrestrial

00:01:48.329 --> 00:01:49.329
invaders.

00:01:49.329 --> 00:01:50.329
"No feds."

00:01:50.329 --> 00:01:51.329
"You'd be better off calling the Ghostbusters,
love."

00:01:51.329 --> 00:01:53.770
The sequel will reunite Boyega and Cornish,
the latter of whom is once again both writing

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:54.950
and directing.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:02:00.590
This time, Boyega will also be acting as co-producer,
in addition to reprising his role as Moses.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:02.340
Speaking to Deadline, Boyega said:

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.819
"It's been a decade since Attack the Block
was released, and so much has changed since

00:02:06.819 --> 00:02:07.819
then.

00:02:07.819 --> 00:02:10.910
I'm excited to see this heightened story return
to the streets of London.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:15.910
Moses has remained one of my favorite characters
to play and bringing him back is a huge honor."

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.980
Cornish echoed his collaborator's enthusiasm,
saying:

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:22.610
"I'm thrilled we're officially announcing
our return to the world of Attack the Block

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.240
on the tenth anniversary of the film's release.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:29.830
I can't wait to work alongside John again,
bringing audiences an even bigger slice of

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.250
inner-city alien action."

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:36.640
Although the Stephen King novel Pet Sematary
has a pretty conclusive ending, the same cannot

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:42.130
be said for the 2019 film adaptation, which
reimagined the story in a much more open-ended

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:43.130
fashion.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:47.280
So it makes sense that Pet Sematary 2 is now
in the works from Paramount, which will be

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.670
helmed by Chaos Walking scribe Lindsey Beer
in her directing debut.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.850
The film is set to skip theaters, debuting
exclusively on the Paramount+ streaming service.

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:03.200
The 2019 remake of the 1989 original starred
Jason Clarke and Amy Seimetz as parents who

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.360
discover a small cemetery near their new house.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:10.700
After their cat is hit by a car and killed,
they bury him in the cemetery, only for him

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:12.140
to come back to life.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:16.570
Of course, everything goes downhill from there,
and, in typical Stephen King fashion, things

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:19.070
get pretty disturbing pretty quickly.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:23.420
Plot details for the sequel are unknown, but
given the ending of the first film, it seems

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:27.480
almost certain that it will feature a new
cast — with the only returning character

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.450
being the Pet Sematary itself.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:33.900
Ahead of the release of Spiral: From the Book
of Saw, the ninth installment in the "Saw"

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.820
horror franchise, star Chris Rock was already
campaigning for a sequel.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.220
Speaking to RadioTimes.com, Rock said:

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.110
"I hope this movie is like Creed.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.910
In the sense that Creed is technically like
Rocky 7.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:48.970
So, hopefully there's more Spirals, and hopefully,
I'm in more Spirals.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.160
[...] We'll see if people like it.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.830
We'll see if people turn out."

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:56.650
Luckily, people have indeed turned out, with
Spiral pushing the horror franchise over the

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.920
$1 billion mark at the global box office.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:03.331
By itself, the numbers for Spiral haven't
been particularly impressive, although it

00:04:03.331 --> 00:04:07.610
hasn't been a disastrous showing by any measure
— especially considering that it was released

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:09.120
in the midst of the COVID-19 pandemic.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:14.370
As such, it was reported ahead of the movie's
release that Lionsgate was actively developing

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:18.350
a tenth Saw film, although this hasn't yet
been confirmed by the studio.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:22.830
And although Spiral director Darren Lynn Bousman
has warned fans not to get ahead of themselves,

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:25.760
he has admitted that a sequel isn't out of
the question.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.540
He told RadioTimes.com:

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:31.070
"I think that [...] if Spiral is successful,
they'll continue it on.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:34.910
But if this has to be successful, fans have
to embrace what this is.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:38.340
And if they do embrace it, I think they'll
continue on as they have in the past."

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.060
The game is afoot — again!

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:46.180
After the smash success of 2020's Enola Holmes,
Netflix's detective caper starring Millie

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:50.650
Bobby Brown as the younger sister of Sherlock
Holmes, the streamer has greenlit a sequel.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:55.660
Based on a series of novels by Nancy Springer,
the first film saw the teenage Enola running

00:04:55.660 --> 00:05:00.440
away from home to investigate her mother's
mysterious disappearance, against the explicit

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:04.620
instructions of her older brother, Mycroft,
who steps in as her guardian.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:09.500
During her journey, she befriends the Viscount
Tewkesbury, a young runaway who's been targeted

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:10.750
for assassination.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:14.880
Of course, by the end of the film, Enola has
solved both mysteries, as well as earned the

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.410
respect of her famous detective sibling.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:22.070
While the plot of the sequel isn't yet known,
it will undoubtedly see Enola taking on another

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:26.570
case, although whether she and Sherlock will
work together this time remains to be seen.

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:30.830
Brown and Henry Cavill will both reprise their
roles for the sequel, which will also bring

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.070
back the original's director, Harry Bradbeer.

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:38.700
At Disney's 2020 Investor Day event, the studio
reaffirmed that a fifth installment in the

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:43.730
iconic Indiana Jones franchise is on the way,
once again starring Harrison Ford.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:46.200
"It's not the years, honey.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.690
It's the mileage."

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:53.000
At 78 years old, Ford will likely be retiring
his trademark whip and fedora by the end of

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:57.530
Indiana Jones 5, although the studio hasn't
yet indicated whether the film will see him

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:01.970
pass the baton to a younger generation — or
close out the franchise for good.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:06.190
However, we do know he'll be joined in his
adventure by Phoebe Waller-Bridge, of Fleabag

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:11.150
fame, and Hannibal's Mads Mikkelsen, along
with Boyd Holbrook and Shaunette Renée Wilson.

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:15.560
And they'll be accompanied by the score of
John Williams, who's also returning for Indy's

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.030
newest adventure.

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:21.110
In the director's chair for Indy 5 is James
Mangold, who has already proved that he is

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:26.200
perfectly capable of bringing the legacy of
a beloved action hero to a dignified end.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:31.230
Mangold previously directed 2017's Logan,
which served as the final adventure for Hugh

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:34.770
Jackman's Wolverine and Patrick Stewart's
Charles Xavier.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:39.730
Logan earned Mangold an Academy Award nomination
for Best Adapted Screenplay and served as

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:44.170
a thrilling and satisfying conclusion for
Jackman and Stewart's characters.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:48.639
While Indiana Jones 5 isn't likely to skew
nearly as dark as Logan, we can only hope

00:06:48.639 --> 00:06:53.520
that it will offer up a suitably moving farewell
to one of cinema's great action icons.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:56.280
The movie hits theaters on July 29th, 2022.

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:02.820
After six successful installments in the found-footage
horror franchise, Paranormal Activity is coming

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:07.270
back with a seventh film, which will once
again partner Paramount Studios with horror

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:09.460
mega-producer Jason Blum.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:14.600
The film will be helmed by Underwater director
Will Eubank from a script by Christopher Landon,

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:19.900
and after a little shuffling due to the COVID-19
pandemic, the decision was made to skip theaters

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:22.840
and release the film directly onto Paramount+.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:26.910
While no plot details have yet been released,
we can take some guesses as to where the movie

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:27.910
is headed.

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:32.699
After the first Paranormal Activity focused
on newlyweds Katie and Micah, every subsequent

00:07:32.699 --> 00:07:36.620
installment has tied back to Katie and her
family in one way or another.

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:41.370
In particular, the Paranormal Activity sequels
most frequently focus on new characters that

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:46.199
happen to encounter Katie and her demonic
companion, Tobi, enabling the franchise to

00:07:46.199 --> 00:07:49.630
tell wider and more intricately intertwined
stories.

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:54.360
It seems almost certain that the seventh movie
will continue this trend in some way, introducing

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:58.520
a new group of characters doomed to have their
lives ruined by Katie and her family.

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:02.950
Keeping with the style of the first six films,
you can also bet your bottom dollar that the

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:06.460
movie will also be presented via a found footage
format.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:07.610
That's kind of the whole point.

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:12.979
Despite the better part of four decades having
passed since The Last Starfighter first wowed

00:08:12.979 --> 00:08:17.550
audiences, the timing may actually be right
for a sequel to the 80s action classic.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:21.699
The original movie follows a teenager who
beats a video game, only to discover that

00:08:21.699 --> 00:08:25.990
said game was really a recruiting tool designed
to find soldiers who can help fight in an

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:27.610
interstellar alien war.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:31.680
Obviously, video games have changed a lot
since then, which could present a natural

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.490
way to continue the story.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:38.169
Speaking to Moviehole, the original movie's
writer Jonathan Betuel said of the sequel:

00:08:38.169 --> 00:08:39.360
"It's not a remake.

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.380
It's going to continue the story.

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:45.889
What's changed is time itself, certainly as
the video world and the alien world have continued

00:08:45.889 --> 00:08:46.949
to tick away.

00:08:46.949 --> 00:08:51.550
It's not a time capsule of the '80s by any
means, we're taking it to the next level.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.140
Passing the torch [...] or the joystick."

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:58.910
Betuel will be co-writing the sequel, titled
The Last Starfighters, with Rogue One screenwriter

00:08:58.910 --> 00:08:59.959
Gary Whitta.

00:08:59.959 --> 00:09:04.749
In March 2021, Whitta tweeted a sizzle reel
containing hints regarding the plot of the

00:09:04.749 --> 00:09:09.629
film, which seems to involve an alien attempting
to assassinate an adult Alex, the protagonist

00:09:09.629 --> 00:09:13.850
of the first film, and Alex then heading off
into space to figure out what's going on.

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:18.390
According to Betuel, the road to making a
sequel has been a rocky one, but he's optimistic

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.050
it will finally get off the ground.

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:21.050
Betuel said:

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:25.639
"I had to go through a process that took years
to recapture the rights, but that was recently

00:09:25.639 --> 00:09:29.970
completed, and although nothing is ever clear
sailing, it looks like we have a really good

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:31.160
opportunity now.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:33.110
So I'm really looking forward to taking it
up."

00:09:34.579 --> 00:09:38.980
Although 2019's wildly fun whodunit Knives
Out was written to be self-contained, director

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:43.809
Rian Johnson wasted no time in letting audiences
know that he'd be open to a sequel, telling

00:09:43.809 --> 00:09:44.809
Collider:

00:09:44.809 --> 00:09:49.010
"If this movie does even okay, I will in a
heartbeat make more of these with Daniel."

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:54.850
As it turned out, Knives Out did a lot better
than okay, bringing in more than $300 million

00:09:54.850 --> 00:10:00.459
worldwide and justifying not one but two sequels,
both of which will go directly to Netflix.

00:10:00.459 --> 00:10:05.300
The move to Netflix is a surprising one, considering
that the first film was distributed theatrically

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:09.879
through Lionsgate, but it was the decision
of both Johnson and his producing partner,

00:10:09.879 --> 00:10:13.910
Ram Bergman, to take the sequels directly
to the streaming site.

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:18.850
Both films will follow Daniel Craig's drawling
private investigator, Benoit Blanc, but he'll

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:21.300
be the only carryover from the first movie.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:25.209
Aside from Craig, Johnson says the Knives
Out sequels will each feature a different

00:10:25.209 --> 00:10:30.600
cast, different setting, and a different donut-shaped
mystery for Blanc to solve, similar to Agatha

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:35.870
Christie's Hercule Poirot novels, which served
as an inspiration for the original movie.

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:39.990
While no release date has been set for either
sequel, the ensemble cast is shaping up to

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:45.199
be every bit as impressive as the first movie,
with Knives Out 2 set to feature with Kathryn

00:10:45.199 --> 00:10:51.290
Hahn, Dave Bautista, Janelle Monae, Leslie
Odom Jr., Edward Norton, and Kate Hudson in

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.399
starring roles.

00:10:52.399 --> 00:10:57.059
"It makes no damn sense.

00:10:57.059 --> 00:10:58.569
Compels me, though."

00:10:58.569 --> 00:11:00.759
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:00.759 --> 00:11:04.589
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:11:04.589 --> 00:11:08.639
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

